// The app's version, the one place it is set. It is the base configuration of the project, so every target inherits it.
// release-please rewrites the line between the markers in each Release PR (release-please-config.json, extra-files);
// tools/release.sh refuses to build a tag whose version differs from the built app's.
// x-release-please-start-version
MARKETING_VERSION = 2.1.0
// x-release-please-end

// The app's name, the same in both builds since 2.1.1 (#759): "Electron Microscopy Studio", the .app, its executable and
// CFBundleDisplayName (Finder, Dock, About, every sentence through AppName.display in TEMCore). App Review refuses "Mac" in an
// App Store app's name (guideline 5.2.5; mac4DSTEM 5.2.0 rejected 16 Nov 2026), and up to 2.1.0 the website download was
// still macEM. The menu bar takes CFBundleName, which Apple keeps short: "Microscopy Studio". The module stays macTEM
// (PRODUCT_MODULE_NAME) and the bundle identifier is unchanged, so settings, recent files, folder grants and updates carry over.
MACEM_APP_NAME_NO = Electron Microscopy Studio
MACEM_APP_NAME_YES = Electron Microscopy Studio
MACEM_MENU_NAME_NO = Microscopy Studio
MACEM_MENU_NAME_YES = Microscopy Studio
MACEM_MENU_NAME = $(MACEM_MENU_NAME_$(MACEM_STORE_BUILD))
